# Cache headers for Workers Static Assets (2026-10-13, the owner's
# "always live" rule made explicit; hardened 2026-10-18 after the owner
# reported the stale-grayscale-page incident on the currena.ir zone):
#
#  - /assets/* are content-hashed by the build — a new deploy changes every
#    hash, so a year-long immutable cache is ALWAYS correct while removing a
#    revalidation round trip per asset. The HTML is the source of truth and
#    it always revalidates, so a cached asset can only ever be one the live
#    HTML itself references.
#  - The document (index.html + the single-page-application fallback paths)
#    revalidates on every request — visitors always get the deployed
#    version. (Workers Assets already send `max-age=0, must-revalidate`
#    for HTML by default; restated so the intent survives config drift.)
#  - /sw.js is NO-STORE (was no-cache): the zone-proxied edge cache
#    (currena.ir) was observed serving a STALE sw.js HIT with no-cache —
#    revalidation at the edge is not trustworthy per-colo, and a stale
#    sw.js freezes every visitor's service worker on the previous deploy
#    (the exact 2026-10-18 "still black and white" report: fresh
#    index.html + stale sw.js manifest = old precache forever). no-store
#    means the edge never keeps a copy — every sw.js fetch hits the
#    worker. The SW script is tiny and fetched once per navigation; the
#    cost is negligible and the update path becomes deterministic.
#  - /api, /internal and /admin are Worker-first paths and set their own
#    headers — untouched here.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-store
